learning_outcomes:
  - Recognise when the Equality Act 2010 applies to a digital scenario, including scenarios involving algorithmic decisions and accessibility
  - Name the nine protected characteristics and identify which one is engaged in a given scenario
  - Distinguish direct discrimination from indirect discrimination and explain when the objective-justification defence may apply
  - Recognise the disability-specific duty to make reasonable adjustments and apply it to accessibility scenarios
